Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_lerc.c
Line: 1005
Function: LERCEncode
Bug type: integer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: num_bytes_needed is computed as an unsigned int: nb_pixels * dst_nbands * (td->td_bitspersample / 8). On large inputs this can wrap around 32-bit, causing an undersized allocation at line 1011. The code then writes nb_pixels * dst_nbands elements into sp->uncompressed_buffer_multiband (e.g., at lines 1029 and 1045), resulting in a heap buffer overflow. This provides a concrete overflow path from a crafted image with very large dimensions/samples-per-pixel.

